  "Question": "Alice is making a batch of cookies and needs \\(2\\frac{1}{2}\\) cups of sugar. Unfortunately, her measuring cup holds only \\(\\frac{1}{4}\\) cup of sugar. How many times must she fill that cup to get the correct amount of sugar?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(8\\)",
    "B": "\\(10\\)",
    "C": "\\(12\\)",
    "D": "\\(16\\)",
    "E": "\\(20\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "One whole cup contains four quarter-cup portions, so the two whole cups require \\(2\\cdot4=8\\) fills. The remaining half cup equals \\(\\frac24\\) cup, requiring two more fills. Thus Alice must fill the cup\n\\[\n8+2=\\boxed{10}\n\\]\ntimes, choice B.",
